## Puja MVP launch policy (SPEC_AMENDMENTS §21) — normative

Read `spec/plans/LAUNCH_POLICY.md` before any dispatch, heartbeat, or booking-flow change.

| Rule | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **Broadcast only** | Never create `dispatch_mode='direct'` at checkout. Do not expose `dispatch-choice`. |
| **Keep DB nets** | **Never drop** `intended_pujari_id`, trigger 3, `ex_bookings_intended_no_overlap`, or `ex_bookings_pujari_no_overlap`. Disabling direct is API/UI only. |
| **No pujari GPS at launch** | `PUT /heartbeat` — lat/lng optional. Dispatch must not `JOIN pujari_live_location` or use `ST_DWithin`. Ship both changes together. |
| **Customer geom** | `addresses.geom` still required at checkout. |
| **Area** | `service_area_id` required on address; display-only on offers — citywide dispatch. |
| **RM** | No customer↔pujari direct phone at launch. Both sides get RM after confirm. |
| **Soft buffer** | `dispatch_buffer_minutes` in eligibility + accept — **not** in exclusion constraint. |
| **Payments (Sprint 1)** | Launch: `payment_mode='booking_fee'` only — Razorpay = frozen `booking_fee` (default ₹61); puja offline. `FULL_ONLINE_ENABLED=false`. Legacy `full_online` / `advance_balance` DDL retained; re-enable via flag + admin. |

Implementation tasks: `plans/STATUS.md` §Puja MVP launch. Migration **012** when implementing schema.

## Dispatch v2 (SPEC_AMENDMENTS §21.6.A–H) — normative

Read `SPEC_AMENDMENTS.md` §21.6.A–H + `DISPATCH_FLOW.md` §Dispatch windows / §Dispatch v2 beat tasks
before any dispatch, booking-gate, offer-TTL, or reconfirmation change. Migration **014**; task
`P-LAUNCH-DISPATCH-V2`.

| Rule | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **Frozen class vs live urgency** | `bookings.booking_class` (`instant`/`advance`) is frozen at `POST /v1/bookings` and drives night gate, offer TTL, RM rules, failure cutoff. Partner-app `urgency` is computed **live** at `GET /v1/offers` (modal vs inbox) — never persisted, never used for policy. Do not conflate them. |
| **Authoritative gate** | `POST /v1/bookings` freezes `booking_class` and applies the night gate (422 `INSTANT_NIGHT_BLOCKED` / `NIGHT_BOOKINGS_DISABLED`) **before** the Razorpay order. `slot-holds` is advisory only. |
| **No recompute at payment** | The webhook reads the frozen class; it does **not** reclassify. It sets `paid_at` + enqueues only — it does **not** compute dispatch windows or write `booking_dispatch_state` (delete that block; the **worker** owns the row + windows). |
| **Class-aware deadline** | Keep `compute_dispatch_windows()` deadlines class-aware (instant `now()+30m`; advance `slot−3h`). Only advance `dispatch_starts_at` moves to `now()` under `immediate_dispatch_on_payment`. Never set a uniform `slot−3h` deadline. |
| **Sibling supersede on accept** | Losing offers are resolved by **trigger 3** (`superseded` + `responded_at`) in the same accept transaction — never an app-layer loop. |
| **Beat tasks off the sweep** | `refresh_advance_offers` (5m), `escalate_urgency_on_threshold` (2m), `rm_escalation_scan` (15m) are separate beat tasks with their own locks. Never add them to the 30s `sweep_task`. Advance-offer refresh is an **in-place `UPDATE expires_at`** (never re-INSERT). |
| **Duration gate** | Do not re-add duration CHECKs (already in migration 006). Rely on trigger 5 + CI assertions; `duration_minutes > 0` is what keeps `ex_bookings_pujari_no_overlap` live. |

